Third-party software (installed as dependencies, not bundled):
- Shapely (BSD 3-Clause) - Geometry operations
- PyProj (MIT) - CRS transformations
- Pydantic (MIT) - Data validation
- HTTPX (BSD 3-Clause) - HTTP client
- FastAPI (MIT) - REST API framework
- Click (BSD 3-Clause) - CLI framework
- Rich (MIT) - Terminal formatting
- NumPy (BSD 3-Clause) - Numerical arrays
- MCP Python SDK (MIT) - Model Context Protocol server

Third-party assets loaded by the web UI from the unpkg CDN (not bundled):
- Leaflet 1.9.4 (BSD 2-Clause) - Interactive maps
- globe.gl 2.33.0 and three-globe 2.33.0 example textures (MIT) - Landing-page globe

Data services queried at runtime. Results derived from them carry the
providers' licences and attribution requirements:
- OpenStreetMap data via Nominatim (geocoding), Overpass API (amenities)
  and map tiles: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
- Copernicus DEM GLO-30 (elevation): produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30
  (c) DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018,
  provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved
- Open Elevation API (elevation fallback): SRTM-derived data
- Open-Meteo (weather and geocoding): CC BY 4.0, https://open-meteo.com/
- OpenAQ (air quality): data from the original providers listed by OpenAQ,
  https://openaq.org/
- NASA FIRMS (active fires): NASA LANCE FIRMS, https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/
- OSRM public demo server (routing): OSRM (BSD 2-Clause) over OpenStreetMap data
- Element 84 Earth Search and Microsoft Planetary Computer (STAC satellite
  catalogues): each collection carries its own licence, e.g. Sentinel-2
  (Copernicus Sentinel data, free and open)

